regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_35.md:89:**So the measuring seat's FLOOR grade of the tile-index family was wrong AS A GRADE, and the codex class-closure review of 2026-09-11 was right** (*"BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30` ... IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT"*).  The data-flow sentence the seat used (*"flows into the address operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does"*) is the 2026-09-09 LABEL clause with its first half dropped: a dispatch LABEL becomes a floor axis when its value flows into a body-read lvalue -- `tlb_mode` is a label the body tests as a case AND flows into `tileptr`; `tile_nr` flows and is not tested as a case.  Flow alone is the transitive-chasing reading the 08-24 bound forbids.
regress/artifacts/fablequeue7n_20261009/fable5_rule7n_35.md:95:**EXHAUSTED / SAMPLED: ADOPTED as clause-(e) disclosure vocabulary, with one correction.**  It is exactly what clause (e) asks for -- *"write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not"* -- made explicit per axis.  Definitions: EXHAUSTED := every cell of the BODY-TESTED partition of that lvalue is rowed (floor discharged on that axis); SAMPLED := driven at two or more values, with the untested slices and their derived or measured sweeps named.  The probe's `:587` wording "every value in the reachable domain is driven" coincides with the partition definition for `tlb_mode`/`bufdepth`/`color_mode` (tiny domains) and must not be the definition: the next probe with a 2^32 operand could never write EXHAUSTED under it and would write it anyway for a 16-value field the body tests at one bound.  BOUND: a disclosure vocabulary can never DEMAND a row (the carrier's filter rule: *"a filter can reject or repair a row; it can never demand a new one"*), so it cannot grow.  STRUCTURAL LANDING SPOT, per the structure-first rule: the PRETABLE block's GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD check gains one column, "partition the BODY induces on this lvalue" (the codex 09-11 table is the exemplar), and EXHAUSTED/SAMPLED is read off that column rather than asserted.  A template line, not a checker.
